  "Question": "If point \\(P\\) is equidistant from the two sides of \\(\\angle AOB\\), must \\(P\\) lie on the angle bisector (\\(P\\) lies inside the angle)?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Yes, it must lie on the angle bisector",
    "B": "Not necessarily; it also depends on the distance from \\(P\\) to the vertex \\(O\\)",
    "C": "Not necessarily; it lies on the angle bisector only when \\(\\angle AOB\\) is a right angle",
    "D": "No, it definitely does not lie on the angle bisector"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A point inside an angle that is equidistant from its two sides lies on the angle bisector. This is the angle bisector criterion.",
